e compound heterozygous variant of APC13 (c.C6A and c.116_126del) from case 3","These APC/C gene mutations all showed a recessive inheritance pattern."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"AR","genotype_reason":"stated for the family"}],"notes":[{"id":"N:40238067:1","pmid":"40238067","section":"molecular_genetics","statement":"Cui et al. (2025) performed whole-exome sequencing in infertile women from 639 unrelated Chinese families and identified 3 probands with biallelic variants in APC/C genes (CDC23 in 2 and APC13 in 1), with phenotypes of oocyte maturation defects, fertilization failure, and early embryonic arrest.","inheritance":"AR","quotes":["We conducted whole-exome sequencing of patients with female infertility from 639 unrelated Chinese families and three probands with APC/C gene mutations were screened.","female infertility characterized by disturbances in oocyte maturation, failure of fertilization, and cessation of early embryonic growth among three distinct Chinese familial lineages"],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:40238067:2","pmid":"40238067","section":"gene_function","statement":"Cui et al. (2025) found in vitro that CDC23 variants resulted in dysregulated protein expression, whereas a missense variant in APC13 was associated with aberrant cellular localization; structural modeling suggested the variants may alter chemical bonds with other APC/C subunits.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["In vitro experimental data suggested that mutations associated with CDC23 result in dysregulated protein expression, whereas missense mutation in APC13 is implicated in aberrant cellular localization patterns.","Structural analysis indicated that these mutations may result in changes in the chemical bonds between themselves and other APC/C subunits."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:37768355:1","pmid":"37768355","section":"molecular_genetics","statement":"Fan et al. (2023) found in vitro that the CDC23 Y329C variant decreased CDC23 protein level, whereas the R330C variant altered the localization of CDC23 in HeLa cells and mouse oocytes.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["In vitro experiments showed that the variant c.986A > G (p.Y329C) led to a decrease in CDC23 protein level and the variant c.988C > T (p.R330C) changed the localization of CDC23 in HeLa cells and mouse oocytes."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:37768355:2","pmid":"37768355","section":"animal_model","statement":"Fan et al. (2023) found that Cdc23 Y329C/Y329C knockin mice mimicked the patients' phenotype, with low expression of CDC23 and APC4 and accumulation of securin and cyclin B1 in oocytes. Treatment with AZ3146 rescued the phenotype.","inheritance":"AR","quotes":["In vivo studies showed that Cdc23Y329C/Y329C mice successfully mimicked the patients' phenotype by causing low expression of CDC23 and APC4 and the accumulation of securin and cyclin B1 in oocytes. AZ3146 treatment was able to rescue the phenotype."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]}],"dropped":{"records":[],"notes":[]},"gene_decisions":{"candidates":["CDC23","ANAPC13"],"confirmed":["CDC23"],"dropped":[],"not_confirmed":["ANAPC13"]},"candidate_inheritance":["AR"]}